In article <1iv87lINNh84@iskut.ucs.ubc.ca>, leffler@physics.ubc.ca (Steve Leffler ) writes:
>   One thing about hack that I'm not clear on is the aggravate monster
>intrinsic.  I seem to see it come up a lot when I die and view my intrinsics.
>Besides eating your dog or wearing a ring of aggravate monster, how do you
>get this intrinsic?  What exactly does it do? I know it makes the monster
>problem worse somehow, but how?  Most importantly, once you've got it, is there
>any way of getting rid of it?

You get the aggravate monster intrinsic by eating a dog, cat, or human corpse
(or elf corpse if you're an elf).

The only way of getting rid of it is getting a gremlin to steal it (not likely).

What it does is wakes up sleeping monsters on your level (leprechauns, nymphs, 
killer bees, zoos full of things, ...)

I believe stealth may (at least partially) offset its effect.
